From e5b3c59b65b79e40277669a5183a5fd2a4480d7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:56:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: make the data depth a build option with the TC1
 ledger derived from it

Ordinary data is retired on credit arrival and the in-flight depth is the
only bound on the frames the firmware holds for the air; at depth 4 the
mean wait from submission to the covering credit was 3.5 ms and every
transmit chunk hit the harness cap. The depth has been a fixed 4 with a
52-page ledger (four frames of 13 pages) since the pipelining proposal,
while the vendor's default budget for the queue is 468 pages. Let a
profile set the depth (1 to 16); the pages the host ledger admits derive
from it, 13 a frame, so a build cannot carry one depth with another
depth's ledger (52 at four, 104 at eight, 156 at twelve). The ledger
still refuses any return that exceeds the debit. Nothing changes at the
default.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/Kconfig | 10 +++++++---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c   | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/Kconfig b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/Kconfig
index 45a166a8c..8b8fcb4c4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/Kconfig
@@ -154,11 +154,15 @@ config MT6797_DATA_CREDIT_RETIRE
 	  transmit completion latency, with its own record on the data end.
 
 config MT6797_CCMP_TX_DEPTH
-	int
+	int "MT6797 Wi-Fi: outstanding ordinary data frames"
 	depends on MT6797_CCMP_TX_PUMP
-	range 1 4
+	range 1 16
 	default 4
 	help
 	  Maximum outstanding ordinary data frames, bounded by PID ownership and
 	  the TC1 page ledger. Management, security and reserved frames keep a
-	  single owner.
+	  single owner. A measurement variable: with ordinary data retired on
+	  credit arrival the depth sets the frames the firmware may hold for
+	  the air. The TC1 ledger admits 13 pages per frame of depth (52 at
+	  the default four, 104 at eight, 156 at twelve) of the firmware's
+	  468-page budget; it derives from this value and cannot disagree.
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
index 3f3cb55d7..1af107aa9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
@@ -17,6 +17,17 @@
 #include <linux/string.h>
 #endif
 #include "hif.h"
+
+/* The TC1 pages the host ledger admits for ordinary data: 13 a full frame
+ * (28-byte descriptor, 1,514-byte Ethernet frame, 128-byte pages) times the
+ * data depth, so the ledger and the depth cannot disagree; 52 without the
+ * depth option, the series' value.
+ */
+#ifdef CONFIG_MT6797_CCMP_TX_DEPTH
+#define MT6797_TC1_LEDGER_PAGES (13U * CONFIG_MT6797_CCMP_TX_DEPTH)
+#else
+#define MT6797_TC1_LEDGER_PAGES 52U
+#endif
 #include "join-submit.h"
 #include "join-command-submit.h"
 
@@ -1013,10 +1024,13 @@ int mt6797_hif_query_capability(struct mt6797_hif *hif, unsigned int sequence,
 	 * their descriptors (13 pages each). The vendor driver's default host
 	 * budget for this queue is 36 such frames (468 pages), and the 26-page
 	 * TC4 pool observed on the device is exactly its two-frame default, so
-	 * four frames stay far inside the firmware's allocation. The ledger
-	 * still refuses any return that exceeds the debit.
+	 * the admitted frames stay inside the firmware's allocation at every
+	 * depth the option allows (13 pages a frame: 52 at four, the series'
+	 * default; 104 at eight; 156 at twelve). The ledger still refuses any
+	 * return that exceeds the debit.
 	 */
-	error = mt6797_normal_admit_tc1(&hif->normal, 52, 52);
+	error = mt6797_normal_admit_tc1(&hif->normal, MT6797_TC1_LEDGER_PAGES,
+					MT6797_TC1_LEDGER_PAGES);
 	if (error)
 		goto out;
 	/* A pre-existing port-1 event would make its reply owner ambiguous.
-- 
2.43.0

